apm-skill-bundle-workaround (Linear CAM-55)

apm 0.29.1 added a staged-download validation gate in
_resolve_downloaded_package whose cascade accepts a native Agent Plugin, a
MARKETPLACE_PLUGIN, a root apm.yml or a root SKILL.md, and otherwise raises
"Downloaded package has no apm.yml or SKILL.md". A SKILL_BUNDLE — nested
skills/<name>/SKILL.md with no root manifest, e.g. the github/gh-stack
dependency of modules/home/ai/plugins/version-control-and-forge — matches no
branch and so fails to install; at 0.29.0 the same shape returned None and the
install proceeded. Still unfixed on 0.30.0 and on microsoft/apm main.

Remove this patch and its overlay once upstream handles PackageType.SKILL_BUNDLE
in that cascade. This patch failing to apply is that signal: either upstream
fixed the cascade, in which case revert the whole apm-skill-bundle-workaround
commit (Linear CAM-55), or upstream only refactored the region, in which case
rebase the hunk.

patch(1) skips leading prose and starts at the first "diff --git" header, so
this preamble is inert under nix's `patch -p1` patchPhase.

diff --git a/src/apm_cli/deps/apm_resolver.py b/src/apm_cli/deps/apm_resolver.py
index e3775ec1..c24bd6fb 100644
--- a/src/apm_cli/deps/apm_resolver.py
+++ b/src/apm_cli/deps/apm_resolver.py
@@ -1274,6 +1274,21 @@ class APMDependencyResolver:
                     downloaded_candidate,
                     had_existing_install,
                 )
+            if package_type is PackageType.SKILL_BUNDLE:
+                # Nested skills/<name>/SKILL.md with no root manifest: a valid
+                # package that carries no transitive dependency metadata.
+                package = APMPackage(
+                    name=dep_ref.get_display_name(),
+                    version="1.0.0",
+                    source=dep_ref.repo_url,
+                    package_path=install_path,
+                    source_path=self._compute_dep_source_path(dep_ref, parent_pkg, install_path),
+                )
+                return self._activate_validated_package(
+                    package,
+                    downloaded_candidate,
+                    had_existing_install,
+                )
             # No manifest found
             self._raise_downloaded_package_error(
                 downloaded_candidate,
